<title>AUSTRALIA: SFE wheat makes new gains in line with Chicago.</title>
<headline>SFE wheat makes new gains in line with Chicago.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian wheat futures strengthened on Wednesday with January 1998 selling 12 lots at A$190.00 a tonne, up A$1.50 on the trade.</p>
<p>Settlement prices strengthened mostly across the board by about A$2.00-A$3.00 a tonne.</p>
<p>Eli Munitz, of Perth Commodities and Futures Brokers Pty Ltd, said that while the market had been quite strong it could be due to ease back slightly.</p>
<p>Wheat futures were being driven mainly by U.S. weather, he said.  </p>
